#!/usr/bin/env python3
# label: Metronome
"""metronome - a metronome with a swinging pendulum and a beat light.

Clicks play through the phone's speaker from the app's sound device: one
continuous stream from `pacat`, with every click placed on its exact sample,
so the beat stays steady however busy the phone is. The pendulum, the beat
boxes and (if you like) the phone's flashlight and vibration follow it.

Set the tempo by tapping (t or Enter) or by clapping into the microphone
(c: clap four or more times, it starts at your tempo, on your beat).

Usage: metronome [BPM]

Keys: space start/stop, Up/Down or + and - tempo ±1, Left/Right ±5,
t or Enter tap tempo, c clap tempo, b and B beats per bar, d subdivision,
a accent on/off, s sound, [ and ] volume, m mute, v vibrate, f flash the
torch, , and . move the picture earlier/later to line up with the sound,
q quit. Settings are kept in ~/.config/metronome/state.json.
"""
